#
# A layout with cameras restarts the camera provider whenever cameraserver starts. The
# provider is lazy: it exits when cameraserver holds no camera, and init starts it
# again through its interface when an application opens one. cameraserver lists only a
# provider that has registered, at its start or later, and nothing else starts a lazy
# AIDL provider the first time, or after it has exited when cameraserver starts again
# (a crash, a restart of the framework). restart, not start: a provider that is still
# running but has unregistered, which a lazy provider does a moment before it exits, is
# not started again by start, and restart starts one that is not running at once. A
# layout without cameras starts none.

